# Kataliya 🌍
### Personal AI Assistant

Kataliya is a personal AI assistant built from the ground up by a solo developer from Durban, South Africa. Inspired by the idea of a real-life Jarvis — a system that handles admin, remembers important information, automates daily tasks, and eventually interacts with the physical world.

This is Act 1. The brain is being built first.

---

## Current Version — Act 1, Version 1

### What Kataliya can do right now:
- Loading screen with animated logo
- Sign in screen
- Personal task dashboard
- Add, delete and complete tasks
- Tasks save permanently to a local database

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, JavaScript |
| Backend | Node.js, Express |
| Database | SQLite (better-sqlite3) |
| Version Control | Git, GitHub |

---

## The Vision

Kataliya is being built in acts:

- **Act 1 (Current)** — The Brain. Software foundation, task management, memory system
- **Act 2** — The Senses. Voice input, notifications, mobile access
- **Act 3** — Physical Interaction. Raspberry Pi hub, connected devices
- **Act 4** — Protection. Non-violent protective presence

---

## Built With AI Assistance

This project was built in collaboration with **Claude** (by Anthropic) as a learning and development tool. Claude assisted with code implementation, debugging, and technical guidance throughout the build process. All product decisions, vision, design, and architecture were made by the developer.

---

## Running Locally

**Prerequisites:** Node.js installed

**Setup:**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/imanathimabunda8-cmyk/Kataliya.git
cd Kataliya
npm install
npm approve-scripts better-sqlite3
node backend/server.js
```

Then open `frontend/index.html` with Live Server in VS Code.

